## In English (read this too)

### What this is

**Modo Jogo Limpo** (Clean Game Mode) is a **helper tool**, written and
published for free so that anyone can free up their computer before playing.

It is **not a virus, not spyware, not adware, and does nothing malicious.**
It sends no data anywhere, opens no ports, does not hide itself, and does not
change the registry without showing you the full list first — and being able
to undo every single change.

### What it actually does

1. **Records** the current state of your computer in a plain text file
   (`snapshot.json`): services, scheduled tasks, registry keys, power plan,
   antivirus exclusions, startup items and shortcuts.
2. **Turns off** the services, tasks, programs and UI elements that consume
   resources while you play.
3. **Restores** everything, item by item, from that file.

In other words: **nothing is destroyed.** Everything that is turned off can be
turned back on, and the app shows you exactly what it is about to turn off
**before** it turns it off.

### Disclaimer and liability

This software is provided **"AS IS"**, without warranty of any kind. The
author accepts **no liability** for:

- any damage to the computer of the person running, recommending or
  redistributing it;
- loss of data, games, settings or work;
- incompatibility with Windows, drivers or third-party software;
- any decision the user makes after using it.

It is the responsibility of the person running it to decide whether to use it,
to test it first, and to back up what matters. Creating a **Windows Restore
Point** before enabling game mode is always a good idea.

### Open source — anyone can read it

The entire source code of this project is **public** under the MIT license
below. Anyone may:

- read, study and copy the code;
- make their own modified version, for themselves or for others;
- help the original project with an issue or a pull request.

Thanks to everyone who wants to contribute. Bug reports and explanations are
worth more than new code.

### AI-assisted development

This application was written, debugged and documented with the help of
**[OpenCode](https://opencode.ai)** and AI language models. All of the code is
available for reading, verification and criticism — including the parts AI
wrote. If you find something wrong, **it is a bug, and bugs get fixed**.

